# Line endings. CI hashes files on a Linux checkout (metadata/distribution_files.json), so a
# Windows checkout that converted text files to CRLF produced a manifest that could never match.
# Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# CSV files are data: keep their bytes exactly as committed (some demo inputs use CRLF, and the
# demo locks hash them).
*.csv -text

# Binary formats: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.docx binary
*.pptx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.xls binary
*.nii binary
*.gz binary
*.dcm binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
